														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2866253">
									

<p>First off, I want to emphasize just how much I love the premise of this. An eldritch entity masquerading as a demonic a-dimensional Mad Max impersonator is just excellent and the way you characterize it in the interview - as somewhat crazed, verging on manically nihilistic - is excellent and allows for an off-kilter feel to pervade the piece, even as it attempts to rectify its 'mistake' with Martha. I can't help but feel that this is unfinished, in that it cuts off abruptly and its ultimate purpose, the memetic effect and what it actually is all remain unresolved. However, I believe that's also to the article's credit: it's an effective example of a work-in-progress, of an item under steady research that is sure to progress in scope but in the meanwhile is a mildly disturbing, decidedly amusing automobile oddity.</p>
<p>+1 for riding shiny and chrome</p>

